  "report": {
    "label": "Report (page numbers, page break)",
    "options": {},
    "template": "<style>\n  @page {\n    margin: 22mm 18mm;\n    @top-left   { content: \"{{ company }}\"; font-size: 10px; color: #555; }\n    @top-right  { content: \"Quarterly report\"; font-size: 10px; color: #555; }\n    @bottom-center { content: \"Page \" counter(page) \" of \" counter(pages); font-size: 10px; color: #555; }\n  }\n  body { font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 12px; color: #222; }\n  h1 { color: #2563eb; } table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }\n  td, th { padding: 5px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; text-align: left; }\n</style>\n<h1>Quarterly report</h1>\n<p>Every page has a header and a numbered footer from the <code>@page</code> rule above. The table below keeps going onto more pages.</p>\n<table>\n  <tr><th>#</th><th>Region</th><th>Orders</th></tr>\n  {% for r in rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.n }}</td><td>{{ r.region }}</td><td>{{ r.orders }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}\n</table>\n\n{% pagebreak %}\n\n<h1>Notes</h1>\n<p>{% pagebreak %} starts a new page, like this one.</p>",
